  "question_stem": "A cyclist starts from rest at a fixed point $O$ and moves in a straight line, before coming to rest $k$ seconds later. The acceleration of the cyclist at time $t$ s after leaving $O$ is $a \\text{ m s}^{-2}$, where $a = 2t^{-\\frac{1}{2}} - \\frac{3}{5}t^{\\frac{1}{2}}$ for $0 < t \\le k$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$k=10\\,\\mathrm{s}$",
    "$4.87\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$ to 3 significant figures (exactly $8\\sqrt{30}/9\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$)."
  ],
